{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>See, I have called by name Betzalel.</b> See, by the holy spirit that is upon you, that Betzalel is fitting for this craft, and you will perceive it by the holy spirit that is upon you. And from the fact that it specifically says 'by name,' hear from this that his name testifies about him, that he was בְּצֵל אֵל (in the shadow of El). Therefore Moses said at the completion of the work of the Mishkan: ״יוֹשֵׁב בְּסֵתֶר עֶלְיוֹן בְּצֵל שַׁדַּי יִתְלוֹנָן״ (Psalms 91:1) — for the makers of the craft were בְּצֵל אֵל. And this is what he concludes, saying: ״כְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר צִוִּיתִיךָ יַעֲשׂוּ״. He did not say that they shall do all that you will command them, but rather they shall do all that I am commanding you — surely then they were בְּצֵל אֵל. And thus Rashi explained in parashat Pekudei on the verse ״וּבְצַלְאֵל בֶּן אוּרִי עָשָׂה כְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר צִוָּה ה׳ אֶת מֹשֶׁה״ (Exodus 38:22). And I wonder why Rashi did not explain this on the verse ״כְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר צִוִּיתִיךָ יַעֲשׂוּ״."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The Kli Yakar cites Psalms 91:1 as Moses's words; the verse's attribution to Moses follows the Midrashic tradition that Moses composed Psalm 91 upon completion of the Mishkan."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:24:35.395511037Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}